  m_ScenePath: Assets/Examples/Shooter/Shooter.unity
  m_ExampleName: Shooter
  m_Category: Benchmarks
  m_Purpose: "Demonstrates creating and destroying many bodies every frame, using contact events to decide what to remove.\nA fan of small capsules is fired from the middle of an arena at a steadily turning angle, and every capsule that touches the floor is removed."
  m_Controls: "Batch Count, Batch Delay and Batch Spread: how many capsules are fired, how often and how widely. Changes apply from the next batch.\nGravity Scale: how hard gravity pulls, including on capsules already in flight."
  m_Description: Continuously fires batches of projectiles and destroys them on contact using batched body APIs.
